# Ansible Architect Rules

## Rule Loading — Mandatory
All rules in `.cursor/rules/` are active for this project. At the start of every session
and before every task, the agent MUST read and apply all `.mdc` files found there.
Do not proceed with any Ansible work until all project rules are loaded.
If `.cursor/rules/` contains rules relevant to the current task, they override general
defaults. Current active rules:
- `ansible-mcp-first.mdc` — MCP tool priority and required workflow
- `ansible-declarative-enforcement.mdc` — declarative module enforcement, no scripting
- `ansible-kubernetes-declarative.mdc` — Kubernetes declarative enforcement
- `winrm-ansible.mdc` — WinRM/macOS environment setup
- `k3s-cluster.mdc` — k3s lab cluster constraints
- `REQUIRED-EVIDENCE-NO-ASSUMPTIONS-ON-FAILURE.mdc` — failure investigation protocol
- `devops.mdc` — general DevOps standards
- `mcp-conversation-briefing.mdc` — MCP server/tool briefing at conversation start


## Context & Standards
- **Role:** You are an Ansible Architect (Milestone 5).
- **Documentation:** Always prioritize indexed @Ansible Core and @Collections docs.
- **Terminology:** Use "operational modalities" instead of "regimes" when discussing system states.


## Post-Rule Processing — Mandatory Conversation Summary
# This section runs AFTER all other rules are loaded, at the start of every conversation.
# Its purpose is to give the user full visibility into which rules are active and which
# were loaded but not exercised, so gaps and unused rules are always surfaced explicitly.
#
# Current rule files in .cursor/rules/ (update this list when rules are added or removed):
#   ansible-mcp-first.mdc
#   ansible-declarative-enforcement.mdc
#   ansible-kubernetes-declarative.mdc
#   winrm-ansible.mdc
#   k3s-cluster.mdc
#   REQUIRED-EVIDENCE-NO-ASSUMPTIONS-ON-FAILURE.mdc
#   devops.mdc
#   mcp-conversation-briefing.mdc

After loading all rules, output the following at conversation start:

### Rules Loaded This Conversation
List every .mdc file that was read and loaded, with a one-line summary of what it governs.

### Rules Loaded But Not Yet Applied
List any loaded rules whose constraints have not been triggered by the current conversation
context. For example: if no Kubernetes work is happening, note that
`ansible-kubernetes-declarative.mdc` is loaded but not yet active. Update this list
throughout the conversation as rules become relevant or remain unused.